label Day3.lavinia
# story entry day=3
# art scene draft.reading.early
# story challenge {"challenge_id":"Day3.lavinia.challenge","playable_marker_id":"Day3.lavinia.playable","end_marker_id":"Day3.lavinia.end","board_profile_id":"week.canonical_solo","targets":{"never_started":"target.Day3.lavinia.result.A","unfinished":"target.Day3.lavinia.result.B","won":"target.Day3.lavinia.result.C","lost":"target.Day3.lavinia.result.D","perfect":"target.Day3.lavinia.result.E"}}
\“Another evening?” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.001
\Inside the coat pocket, Sylvia's fingers stay over mine for one more second, then open and let my hand slip back into the cool air. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.002
\“Perhaps,” she says, and turns up the hill path with her sketchbook under her arm; the library quad lies the other way. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.003
\By six o'clock, the florist paper around the white flowers has grown damp beneath the thumb. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.004
\Lavinia's fingers ease one creased petal out of the paper fold. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.005
\“You're bruising them.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.006
\“I was holding them out of the wind for you.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.007
\“By strangling the stems?” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.008
\“They survived the walk up the hill.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.009
\The wrapping slides through my fingers, though one small white blossom catches on a nail. Lavinia takes that one too, tucks the stem back into the center of the bunch, and looks up with the corner of her mouth lifting. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.010
\“There.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.011
\“You're welcome.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.012
\She buries her face in the white heads until her eyes are hidden behind the paper rim. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.013
\“Where are you taking me?” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.014
\“Left.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.015
\Past the corner of the library wall, she keeps the bouquet lifted under her nose while I pace half a step beside her right shoulder—slowing the cadence before the flagstones dip so her right ankle never has to take an uneven drop. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.016
\“Which way now?” she asks from behind the flowers. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.017
\A silent gesture toward the hedge path. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.018
\“Say it aloud. I can't see through your bribe.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.019
\“Right. Mind the curb.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.020
\“I know where the curb is.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.021
\“You walked into it in February.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.022
\“Because you were talking.” She lowers the paper an inch, laughing. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.023
\Directly ahead, the main library steps rise back into view from the opposite side. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.024
\“A remarkably short walk, Priscilla.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.025
\“The first lap is to make sure you're paying attention. I know a longer way.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.026
\“I'm sure you do.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.027
\She shifts the flowers into the crook of her left arm and slips her right hand into mine—fingers warm, thumb settling over the back of my knuckle as if rewarding the first lap. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.028
\A little longer like this. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.029
\Beyond the side arch, the flagstones narrow. A parked bicycle leans across half the path. Turning sideways so her hip won't brush the wet hedge, Lavinia lets the white flower heads strike the metal bell; it gives a single, unfinished ring. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.030
\“Excuse us,” she tells the handlebars. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.031
\“There was room on the grass.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.032
\“It had no business parking in the middle.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.033
\Her hand stays laced in mine behind her hip until the path opens onto the iron gate. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.034
\Under the gate lamp, two figures stop mid-stride—a cardigan swinging from a wrist, two takeaway cups balanced in the other hand. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.035
\“We're walking down for coffee. Come with us for half an hour.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.036
\A glance toward Lavinia. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.037
\“If you like,” she says evenly. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.038
\“We could come for a little—” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.039
\Inside the joined hands, Lavinia's grip closes all at once—pressing the ring finger hard against the middle knuckle. When my hand instincts to ease back half an inch, she does not release it; she twists the wrist a fraction inward against the damp flower stems so my breath catches audibly in the middle of the word. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.040
\An extravagant way to train someone not to look toward the gate\: she is creasing her own stems against my cuff to do it. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.041
\“One moment,” I say toward the lamp, and turn half a step inward. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.042
\“Let go.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.043
\Her fingers uncurl slowly. For half a beat the palms stay stuck together by the damp warmth of the skin; separating them hurts sharper than the grip did. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.044
\“That hurt.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.045
\“I wanted an evening with you.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.046
\Under the gate lamp, the figure with the cardigan waits for the answer. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.047
\Accept the invitation for both of us. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.048
