label Day3.lavinia.result.C
# story entry day=3
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“Yes,” I say toward the gate, and then turn to Lavinia\: “Will you come for one cup?” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.001
\“You asked for a walk.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.002
\“Both are possible.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.003
\“How long is one cup?” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.004
\“Until it cools.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.005
\She looks through the iron bars, then settles the flowers higher against her shoulder. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.006
\“One cup.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.007
\At the narrow café table, four chairs fit badly; Lavinia draws hers flush against mine and lays the white bouquet across her knees so the paper rim rises above the tabletop. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.008
\“You'll have to look around them,” she says. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.009
\“I have been.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.010
\A place beside me, even in company. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.C.011
label Day3.lavinia.result.C.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day4"}}
