label Day3.lavinia.result.D
# story entry day=3
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“We'll come,” I say toward the gate. “Give her a moment. She'll come.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.001
\“I'm not going,” Lavinia says. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.002
\“You aren't interrupting—” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.003
\Lavinia hurls the bouquet straight down between us; the heavy wet stems strike across my ankles before the paper splits open against the flagstones. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.004
\Two white heads snap cleanly from their stalks; another rolls into the mud beside the base of the iron rail. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.005
\Under the lamp, the voice at the gate cuts off mid-syllable. A knee bends as if to reach for the nearest flower. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.006
\“Leave them,” Lavinia says, her voice flat and exact. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.007
\The figure straightens. The gate latch catches once, misses, and clicks shut as both shadows hurry away down the hill. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.008
\“Go on,” Lavinia says, her hands empty at her sides, chest rising fast beneath her unbuttoned collar. “Smile at them. Catch up.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.009
\“They were for you.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.010
\“I know.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.011
\Both knees touch the damp paving stones right at her feet. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.012
\“I said leave them.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.013
\“No. The paper is only torn to the middle.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.014
\She threw her own gift into the mud just to clear the gate in ten seconds. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.015
\As fingers reach past her instep for the snapped stems, her right shoe slides half an inch backward—not retreating toward the gate, only lifting the hem of her coat so the wool won't brush my cuff in the dirt. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.016
\“That one won't stay,” she says, looking down at the broken white head by the rail. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.017
\“Hold this.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.018
\She does not touch the loose blossom. Instead, she bends from the waist and takes the two corners of the torn wrapping from my fingers, holding the paper open like a pocket while I lay the bruised stems back inside. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.019
\When we stand, she presses the ruined bunch between our coats with one forearm. Her other hand comes up to the back of my neck—fingers cool and damp from the torn florist paper—and pulls my head forward until her forehead rests hard against my shoulder. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.020
\Keep hold of me. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.021
\“Answer for me in front of people again,” she whispers into the wool of my shoulder, her fingers tightening at my nape, “and it won't be the flowers next time.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.022
\“You helped me pick them up.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.023
\She laughs once against my collarbone—a short, breathless sound—and does not let go of my neck as the torn paper crackles between our chests. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.D.024
label Day3.lavinia.result.D.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day4"}}
return

label Day3.lavinia.result.E
# story entry day=3
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“Yes,” I say toward the gate, and then turn to Lavinia\: “Will you come for one cup?” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.001
\“You asked for a walk.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.002
\“Both are possible.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.003
\“How long is one cup?” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.004
\“Until it cools.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.005
\She looks through the iron bars, then settles the flowers higher against her shoulder. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.006
\“One cup.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.007
\At the narrow café table, four chairs fit badly; Lavinia draws hers flush against mine and lays the white bouquet across her knees so the paper rim rises above the tabletop. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.008
\“You'll have to look around them,” she says. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.009
\“I have been.” #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.010
\A place beside me, even in company. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.011
\Someone is listening. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.012
\None of the faces around this table. Somewhere the eyes cannot place. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.013
\You. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.014
\The wish to bring her here was mine. It remains mine. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.015
\The porcelain cup turns once beneath the fingertips. #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.016
\What, exactly, have you been waiting to see? #id:line.Day3.lavinia.result.E.017
label Day3.lavinia.result.E.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day4"}}
return

label Day3.sylvia.result.A
# story entry day=3
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“Come out to the balcony for a minute. When the light cycle finishes.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.001
\“Let the attic bulb come on first.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.002
\The tiny landing light dims; three seconds later, the attic window goes dark. Sylvia lifts our joined hands. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.003
\“Now?” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.004
\“Now.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.005
\Outside in the cool corridor, she leans one shoulder against the wall. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.006
\“What did you want to show me?” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.007
\“Nothing in the case.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.008
\“I was comfortable on that stool.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.009
\“Only after I held it down.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.010
\She offers her arm; we step back inside before the miniature house lights begin their next cycle. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.A.011
label Day3.sylvia.result.A.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day4"}}
return

label Day3.sylvia.result.B
# story entry day=3
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“Nothing.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.B.001
\Sylvia glances sideways, then back at the lit cross-section house. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.B.002
\“You nearly made me miss the timer.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.B.003
\Her fingers tighten once around my palm, then relax. For ten minutes the tiny bulbs inside the miniature rooms switch on and off in sequence—attic, landing, under-stair cupboard—while her little finger stays hooked against mine under the shared coat. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.B.004
label Day3.sylvia.result.B.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day4"}}
return

label Day3.sylvia.result.C
# story entry day=3
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“Come out into the corridor with me for a minute.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.001
\“Why?” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.002
\“I'd rather talk to you than look at a wooden house.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.003
\Sylvia looks from the lit miniature staircase to my mouth, then smiles. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.004
\“All right.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.005
\In the quiet corridor outside the door, she leans beside the window. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.006
\“Well?” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.007
\“I like being out with you.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.008
\“You cancelled a walk to tell me that in a hallway.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.009
\“The lighting is better out here.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.010
\She laughs softly and opens her palm beside mine. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.011
\“We can walk the long way back when the building closes,” she says. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.012
\After the building closes. There is an after. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.C.013
label Day3.sylvia.result.C.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day4"}}
return

label Day3.sylvia.result.D
# story entry day=3
# art scene draft.reading.early
\“Come outside with me.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.001
\“Wait until the landing light changes.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.002
\“Now.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.003
\The hand pulls free of hers. The folding stool snaps up behind the knees as two steps carry me into the narrow space directly between her stool and the illuminated glass case. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.004
\My coat blocks the cross-section house completely, throwing a dark rectangle across her knees and glasses. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.005
\Sylvia tilts her head back to look up. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.006
\“Sit down, Priscilla.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.007
\“I didn't cancel six o'clock to watch you look at someone else.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.008
\Her eyes stay on my face for a full beat. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.009
\“The two-inch man in the cupboard?” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.010
\“Come outside.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.011
\The light from the miniature house behind my back catches the corner of Sylvia's mouth. She takes her coat, stands sideways off the stool, and walks out into the corridor. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.012
\As the door swings shut behind us, she turns and pushes her coat into my hands. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.013
\“Hold that.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.014
\She smooths her cardigan cuff—and then laughs, a short, clear sound against the quiet wall. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.015
\“What?” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.016
\“You stood in front of a wooden model.” She shakes her head, still smiling. “You looked ridiculous.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.017
\“You were looking at it.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.018
\“I couldn't see anything else with your coat in the way.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.019
\“Stay out here a minute.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.020
\The laugh stops. She takes her coat back slowly, without taking her eyes off mine. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.021
\“If you're going to interrupt the whole evening, Priscilla, you'd better have something else prepared.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.022
\“I don't.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.023
\“Then you'd better hold my attention.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.024
\“How?” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.025
\“Something better than the little house.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.026
\Nothing prepared. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.027
\Her smile widens. She steps under the corridor lamp and slides her right hand back into mine—palm to palm, her thumb pressing steadily against the inside of my wrist, leaving a faint grey trace of afternoon pencil lead directly over the pulse. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.028
\“There,” she says softly. “Now look.” #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.029
\Behind the closed door, the timer relay clicks and the miniature house resets in the dark. Her eyes do not leave mine. #id:line.Day3.sylvia.result.D.030
label Day3.sylvia.result.D.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day4"}}
return

